Teach curl's bundled `config.sub` about Apple's iOS-simulator host triplet.

`build.sh` configures curl with `--host=$HOST_TRIPLET`, and forge builds three
iOS slices: `arm64-apple-ios` (device), `arm64-apple-ios-simulator` and
`x86_64-apple-ios-simulator`. autoconf pushes every `--host` value through the
`config.sub` shipped in the tarball (curl 8.11.0 carries the 2022-01-03
vintage) before a single file is compiled. That script splits the four-field
name into machine `<cpu>-apple` plus OS `ios-simulator`, then splits the OS on
its dash into kernel `ios` and OS `simulator`. The bare word `simulator` gets
past the list of recognised OS names only by accident -- it matches the
unrelated `sim*` entry meant for bare-metal simulator targets -- and then
reaches the block that validates kernel/OS *pairs*. That block has no case for
`ios` + `simulator`, so it falls through to its catch-all and configure stops
with

    Invalid configuration `arm64-apple-ios-simulator': Kernel `ios' not known
    to work with OS `simulator'.

Nothing is compiled, so the failure looks nothing like a build error. The
device triplet `arm64-apple-ios` canonicalises fine, and so does every Android
triplet; only the two simulator slices die. That split is the tell.

The patch adds an empty `ios-simulator)` case to that kernel/OS pairing block,
alongside the existing `*-eabi*` entry -- i.e. "this pairing is valid, no
normalisation needed". Nothing else changes: `arm64-apple-ios-simulator` now
canonicalises to `aarch64-apple-ios-simulator`, and the device and Android
triplets canonicalise exactly as they did before.

Without this, two of the three iOS slices of flet-libcurl never get past
configure, and everything downstream of it (flet-libproj, and through it
flet-libgdal / pyproj) loses its iOS wheels. Android is unaffected.

The commit that introduced this file (ec8d184, a bulk branch consolidation)
records no rationale; the account above is reconstructed from the diff and
confirmed by running curl's own config.sub against forge's triplets, patched
and unpatched.

diff --git a/config.sub b/config.sub
index dba16e8..215b8e2 100755
--- a/config.sub
+++ b/config.sub
@@ -1792,6 +1792,8 @@ case $kernel-$os in
 		;;
 	*-eabi* | *-gnueabi*)
 		;;
+	ios-simulator)
+		;;
 	-*)
 		# Blank kernel with real OS is always fine.
 		;;
